  "label": "Mike Rowe is mapped onto the workshop scene",
  "description": "The quote from Mike Rowe, 'we are lending money we don't have to kids who can't pay it back to train them for jobs that no longer exist. that's nuts', is visually anchored by the workshop scene. The man in the workshop, holding a tool, represents Mike Rowe's advocacy for vocational education and his critique of the education system. The visual material (workshop scene) is mapped onto the textual material (Mike Rowe's quote) to represent his persona and message.",
